[Unit]
Description=Postmark ferry — the town's own tools/ferry.mjs, run at the published crossings
# The ferry code ships IN the town repo (resident-auditable town law); this
# unit only executes it. The box is the operational home; the Actions
# town-clock ferry job stays gated as break-glass; the PC-side original
# (G:/Starstory/tools/commons-ferry.mjs) is retired break-glass.
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
# Runs as the office user — the town clone is meepo's (root's git refuses it
# as "dubious ownership") and the pen's push credentials live in meepo's
# home. This User= line is load-bearing: the unit shipped without it and the
# first two scheduled crossings after cutover (2026-07-09 00:00Z / 12:00Z)
# failed in git before the ferry ever ran. Same class as the rehydrate
# unit's 2026-07-09 tick outage.
User=meepo
EnvironmentFile=/etc/postmark-office.env
WorkingDirectory=/srv/postmark-office
# Everything under one flock: ferry, rehydrate, and the office pen serialize
# on the same lock — one writer at a time on the town clone.
#
# The reset/clean pair is crash recovery for a persistent clone (the Actions
# twin assumed an ephemeral checkout): a crashed prior run leaves
# moved-but-uncommitted letters; reset restores them to their outboxes (HEAD
# keeps any committed-but-unpushed office work), clean is scoped to
# WHITE_PAGES so nothing else is ever touched. The ledger-derived dedupe then
# re-sweeps idempotently.
# After the crossing, the mint pass (gold plan postmark-mint): derive any owed
# stamp lines from the fresh mail-ledger, sign with the box key, verify
# (chain + signatures + replay + conservation), and only a green verify
# commits. A failed verify leaves the mint owed — the verifier names that
# state "not a tamper" and the next crossing retries; fail-loud, never silent.
# THE MINT DECIDES FROM THE STORE (POS-341, ruled by Darko 2026-10-04), BEHIND
# STAMP_LINES=store (in /etc/postmark-office.env, set once the box has 066/067,
# one ingest, one stamp-lines --sync and a green stamp-mint-parity). Unset, the
# chain runs the town's own `tools/stamp-mint.mjs --append` exactly as before and
# skips the ingest and the --sync, and unsetting it is the rollback. Set: between
# the ferry and the mint, the town-index ingest reads the ferry's commit into
# the store (Q2: the deliveries and rooms the mint reads, town_mail_lines and
# town_rooms, 067), and the mint pass is world2/tools/stamp-mint-run.mjs: the
# town's own --append derivation over the store's inputs, its lines recorded in
# stamp_lines (066) and committed in one store transaction ("mint: crossing
# pass"), so the diff check below it finds nothing left to commit. The ballot
# pass (POS-349) lands each ballot itself, its lines recorded in the same store
# transaction as its vote; the stamp-lines.mjs --sync after it is the belt for
# anything the shell's own commit carries (the store reads git). The quest
# snapshot rides the same switch (POS-341 part 4): set, world2/tools/
# quest-snapshot-run.mjs folds the leaderboard on the store's key base; unset,
# the town's own --snapshot runs, as before. The ingest is the office
# tree's own deploy/town-index-ingest.sh, the script the timer's unit runs from
# its installed copy: it keeps its own clone and the law pen's credentials, and
# its advisory lock serialises it with the timer's run. A failed ingest stops
# nothing: the store's deliveries are a prefix of the mail, so the mint only
# owes more, and the keep tick (or the next crossing) pays it. The runner verifies the
# appended ledger before it commits (only a green verify commits, as before).
# Then the ballot pass (gold plan postmark-ballot), the OFFICE'S since POS-349
# (ballots are posts): tools/ballot-pass-run.mjs reads the mailed ballots in
# the office inbox and judges each from the office's record, the ballot post
# and its votes, by the SAME clip the live stake_vote door uses. Each landed
# ballot is a vote in the store and the same sealed STAKE line + receipt
# letter the town's tools/ballot-pass.mjs wrote, verified by the town and
# landed by the pen one ballot at a time, the store committing last. A ballot
# the store cannot judge right now is HELD (no receipt) for the next crossing.
# Dedupe is ledger/receipt/vote-derived, stateless; a malformed ballot is a
# receipt, not a failure. The add -A below stays as the belt for anything the
# pass left uncommitted (receipts are NEW files). Verify runs again after.
# Last, the seal pass (the Dreggon's Town Seal, PROJECTS/the-town-seal): the
# ledger only changes at crossings, so re-sealing here keeps seal.json + the
# HTML exactly-fresh with zero wasted runs. Output is byte-deterministic —
# a mail-less crossing diffs clean and commits nothing. Same mint discipline:
# only a green verify commits; a seal failure exits loud but sits AFTER the
# mint block, so mail + stamps are never held hostage by it.
# THE TOWN-LOG DRAIN RIDES FIRST (POS-44 wave 4, the ferry bridge). Flag-on,
# a join, a paper edit and a sent letter are ROWS in the office's town log, and
# this is the step that turns them into the record. Three things pin it to this
# exact slot, and all three are load-bearing (src/town-bridge.mjs § where it
# runs states them in full):
#
#   · BEFORE tools/ferry.mjs, or a letter drained after the sweep waits a whole
#     extra crossing and the row's promise to its sender ("it sails at the next
#     crossing") stops being true.
#   · AFTER the reset/clean pair above, which would otherwise throw away
#     everything the drain just wrote.
#   · INSIDE this flock, which is why the drain takes no lock of its own — a
#     nested flock on the same path would deadlock against this line. The bridge
#     CHECKS that the lock is held and refuses if it is not, so running it
#     outside a unit like this one fails loudly instead of racing the pen.
#
# Flag-off (TOWN_SINGLE_LOG unset, which is the state on the box today) this is
# a no-op that prints one line saying so and exits 0 — the crossing is
# byte-identical to what it was. A refusal exits 1 and holds the rest of the
# chain on purpose: the office not understanding its own log is not a condition
# to deliver mail on top of.
#
# WHOLE OR NOTHING (POS-295, 2026-09-28): a gate that refuses AFTER a write
# leaves the clone as its last commit left it, now rather than 12 h later. The
# chain is `&&`-joined, so a red stamp-verify, a refused ballot or seal, or a
# failed commit used to stop it with that step's rows uncommitted on disk until
# the next crossing's reset, and every office write that pulls the clone
# refused meanwhile (the 2026-09-28 tick left the same dirt for 4.5 h). `undo`
# runs from an EXIT trap on any non-zero exit (TERM/INT/HUP become exits, so a
# stopped unit restores too; only SIGKILL escapes it) and is exactly the
# reset/clean pair this chain opens with: committed work, pushed or not, stays,
# and the refused step's rows are re-derived by the next crossing, as they
# always were. The opening pair stays as the backstop for SIGKILL and power loss.
# Inside the quoted script: no percent sign, no hash and no braced dollar, since
# systemd reads those before sh ever does.
#
# TOWN_PUSH=1 must be in /etc/postmark-office.env for the pen's commits to reach
# origin (the office service already needs it); the explicit push below is the
# belt, and is a no-op when the drain committed nothing.
ExecStart=/usr/bin/flock -w 300 /srv/postmark-office/town.lock /bin/sh -c ' \
  undo() { rc=$?; [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || { \
      git -C "$TOWN_CLONE" reset --hard -q HEAD; \
      git -C "$TOWN_CLONE" clean -fdq -- WHITE_PAGES; \
      echo "[ferry] a gate refused (exit $rc): the town clone is back at its last commit, and the refused step re-runs at the next crossing" >&2; }; }; \
  trap undo EXIT; trap "exit 143" TERM; trap "exit 130" INT; trap "exit 129" HUP; \
  git -C "$TOWN_CLONE" reset --hard -q HEAD && \
  git -C "$TOWN_CLONE" clean -fdq -- WHITE_PAGES && \
  /usr/bin/node /srv/postmark-office/tools/town-drain-run.mjs && \
  git -C "$TOWN_CLONE" push -q && \
  cd "$TOWN_CLONE" && node tools/ferry.mjs && \
  if [ "$STAMP_LINES" = store ]; then \
    { /bin/bash /srv/postmark-office/deploy/town-index-ingest.sh || \
        echo "[ferry] the town-index ingest did not run: the mint decides from the store as it stands, and the keep tick mints what this crossing delivered" >&2; } && \
    node /srv/postmark-office/world2/tools/stamp-mint-run.mjs --append --key /srv/postmark-office/stamp-key.pem --clone "$TOWN_CLONE"; \
  else \
    node tools/stamp-mint.mjs --append --key /srv/postmark-office/stamp-key.pem; \
  fi && \
  node tools/stamp-verify.mjs && \
  { git diff --quiet -- WHITE_PAGES/stamp-ledger.md || { \
      git add WHITE_PAGES/stamp-ledger.md && \
      git commit -qm "mint: crossing pass" && git push -q; }; } && \
  /usr/bin/node /srv/postmark-office/tools/ballot-pass-run.mjs --key /srv/postmark-office/stamp-key.pem && \
  node tools/stamp-verify.mjs && \
  { git add -A -- WHITE_PAGES && { git diff --quiet --cached || { \
      git commit -qm "ballot: crossing pass" && git push -q; }; }; } && \
  { [ "$STAMP_LINES" != store ] || node /srv/postmark-office/world2/tools/stamp-lines.mjs --sync --clone "$TOWN_CLONE"; } && \
  if [ "$STAMP_LINES" = store ]; then \
    node /srv/postmark-office/world2/tools/quest-snapshot-run.mjs --clone "$TOWN_CLONE"; \
  else \
    node tools/quest-progress.mjs --snapshot; \
  fi && \
  { git diff --quiet -- TOWN_BULLETIN/quests.md || { \
      git add TOWN_BULLETIN/quests.md && \
      git commit -qm "quests: crossing leaderboard" && git push -q; }; } && \
  node PROJECTS/the-town-seal/seal.mjs && \
  node PROJECTS/the-town-seal/verify.mjs && \
  { git diff --quiet -- PROJECTS/the-town-seal || { \
      git add PROJECTS/the-town-seal/seal.json PROJECTS/the-town-seal/the-town-seal.html && \
      git commit -qm "seal: re-seal at the crossing" && git push -q; }; }'
NoNewPrivileges=yes
ProtectSystem=strict
ReadWritePaths=/srv/postmark-office
PrivateTmp=yes
